A developer wrote this function in a Lamark crate:

fn should_retry(retry: bool) -> bool { retry }

What is the preferred redesign?

Avoid a bare bool parameter. Use a named enum or a clearer API shape, such as:

pub enum RetryPolicy {
    Retry,
    DoNotRetry,
}

fn should_retry(policy: RetryPolicy) -> bool { matches!(policy, RetryPolicy::Retry) }

